{
  "dom_id": "questionExplanation-166812",
  "name": null,
  "problem": "",
  "worked_solution": "To determine the amount of additive that Mike must dissolve in $2.5$ liters of paint, we must multiply $6.5$ by $2.5.$\n\nWe proceed by multiplying the two numbers just as we would with whole numbers.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & \\begin{aligned} &  &  &  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\begin{aligned}\\boxed{1} \\\\ \\boxed{2}\\end{aligned}\\,\\,\\,\\,\\, & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\begin{aligned}\\boxed{} \\\\ \\boxed{4}\\end{aligned}\\,\\,\\,\\, &  \\\\  &  &  &  & \\,\\,\\,\\,6\\,\\,\\,\\, & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,.5\\,\\,\\,\\, \\\\ \\,\\,\\,\\,\\times \\,\\,\\,\\, & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\, & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\, & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\, & \\,\\,\\,\\,2\\,\\,\\,\\, & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,.5\\,\\,\\,\\, \\\\  &  &  & \\,\\,\\,\\,3\\,\\,\\,\\, & \\,\\,\\,\\,2\\,\\,\\,\\, & \\,\\,\\,\\,5\\,\\,\\,\\, \\\\ \\,\\,\\,\\,+\\,\\,\\,\\, & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\, & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,1\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\, & \\,\\,\\,\\,3\\,\\,\\,\\, & \\,\\,\\,\\,0\\,\\,\\,\\, & \\,\\,\\,\\,0\\,\\,\\,\\, \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\, & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,1\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\, & \\,\\,\\,\\,6\\,\\,\\,\\, & \\,\\,\\,\\,2\\,\\,\\,\\, & \\,\\,\\,\\,5\\,\\,\\,\\,\\end{aligned}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe now count the total number of decimal places in the two factors.\n\nThere is $1$ decimal place in $6.5$ and there is $1$ decimal place in $2.5.$\nTherefore, their product will have $1+1=2$ decimal places.\n\nSo, we take our value of $1625$ and add a decimal point to make a number with $2$ decimal places.\n\n$$\n16\\,\\overset{↓}{.}\\,\\,\\,{{25}_{⏟}}_{2\\text{ digits}}\n$$\n\nHence, $6.5\\times 2.5=16.25.$\n\nWe conclude that Mike must use $16.25$ grams of additive.",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
